{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/1/codegen_prompts/7.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1852178230/1`\n- 题号：`7`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/1/7.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"7\">\n- `description`：在被色框分隔的子区域中，每个区域内的散点图案需要被\"传送\"到由隐藏配对规则指定的另一个区域，配对规则由框的边长奇偶性决定。\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有偶数个（如 4 个或 6 个）不重叠的单色空心矩形框，每个框的颜色各不相同。每个框内部（框线以内的区域）包含一组由某种非框色、非背景色的颜色绘制的散点图案（连通或不连通均可），不同框内的散点图案颜色也各不相同。\n- `Rule`：第一步——框的配对：将所有框按照边长奇偶性分组。具体地，计算每个框的宽度（列数）和高度（行数）。将\"宽为奇、高为奇\"的框归为一组，\"宽为偶、高为偶\"的框归为一组，\"宽为奇、高为偶\"归为一组，\"宽为偶、高为奇\"归为一组。每组内恰好有两个框，它们构成一对。第二步——图案交换：对于配对的两个框 A 和 B，将 A 内部的散点图案（保持相对于 A 框左上角内侧的偏移不变）搬移到 B 的内部（以 B 框左上角内侧为锚点，相同偏移放置），同时将 B 的散点图案搬到 A 内。散点图案保持原来的颜色不变。框本身保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：框的配对规则隐藏在框的几何属性中——宽高的奇偶组合将框两两配对。解题者需要先发现\"哪个框的内容去了哪里\"（观察图案的形状在不同框间的交换），再从框的尺寸中归纳出配对依据是宽高奇偶性的组合匹配，最后理解图案是以锚点对齐方式搬移的。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/89565ca0, train/5a719d11, train/df9fd884, train/57edb29d, eval/8f215267, train/e734a0e8, eval/581f7754, train/d968ffd4\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"89565ca0\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3789\nmechanism=0.5096\nlexical=0.0118\ncode_feature=0.2500\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:translate, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/89565ca0.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/89565ca0.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nConvert each colored partitioned frame into a horizontal bar whose length is its number of enclosed regions.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black background with several axis-aligned colored line drawings.\n- The line drawings are damaged by scattered pixels of one non-background noise color and by overlaps with other drawings.\n- Each real drawing is a rectangular partitioned frame enclosing one or more background regions.\n\nRule:\n- For each non-background color, reconstruct its horizontal and vertical wall segments from dense row/column evidence.\n- Count the 4-connected background regions fully enclosed by those reconstructed walls.\n- The color with no enclosed region is the noise/pad color.\n- Sort drawing colors by enclosed-region count; equal counts are ordered by which reconstructed frame covers the other.\n\nKey insight:\n- The scattered color is not an object; it only pads the histogram, while each true object's room count is stable after rectilinear wall reconstruction.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"colored partitioned frame line drawings; ignore scattered pad-color pixels\",\n  \"dst\": \"stack one horizontal bar per frame, ordered by count of enclosed background regions then color id\",\n  \"transform\": \"bar length = number of enclosed 4-connected background regions; pad right with the scattered color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"height = number of frame colors, width = maximum enclosed-region count\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5a719d11\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3526\nmechanism=0.4645\nlexical=0.0125\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, object:axis, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:translate, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5a719d11.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/5a719d11.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nWithin each horizontal pair of two-color panels, swap the motif masks and recolor each pasted mask with the source panel's base color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A separator color forms full blank rows and at least one full blank column.\n- The non-separator area is split into row bands, each containing exactly two same-shaped rectangular panels.\n- Each panel has a dominant base color and one minority motif color.\n\nRule:\n- For every row band, clear each panel to its own base color.\n- Paste the right panel's motif mask into the left panel using the right base color.\n- Paste the left panel's motif mask into the right panel using the left base color.\n\nKey insight:\n- The motif colors themselves are distractors; only each motif's shape mask and the two panel base colors are exchanged.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"minority-color motif mask s inside a two-color panel\",\n  \"dst\": \"horizontally paired panel d in the same row band\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.panel and d are paired across the separator columns within the same row band\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear d to its dominant base color and draw s using s.panel base color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"df9fd884\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3329\nmechanism=0.4355\nlexical=0.0125\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:translate, output:same_size, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/df9fd884.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/df9fd884.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the colored object from the lower bracket lane to the upper bracket lane and drop it to the bottom edge.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One frame color forms exactly two 4-connected bracket objects: a top-edge bracket open downward and a bottom-edge bracket open upward.\n- One other 4-connected foreground object sits in the lower bracket's interior column span.\n\nRule\n- Remove the movable object from its original cells.\n- Keep its shape and color unchanged.\n- Paste it with its bbox columns aligned to the top bracket's interior columns and with its bbox bottom aligned to the grid bottom.\n\nKey insight\n- The lower bracket identifies the object's source lane; the upper bracket provides the target lane, and the final vertical placement is bottom-aligned.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"monochromatic foreground object s whose bbox columns match the lower bracket interior\",\n  \"dst\": \"bottom-aligned slot d in the upper bracket interior column span\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.width == d.width; lower bracket gives the source lane and upper bracket gives d.columns\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear s; translate it unchanged into d with s.bbox.bottom aligned to the grid bottom\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"57edb29d\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3078\nmechanism=0.3735\nlexical=0.0121\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:axis, object:frame, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:shape_match, operation:translate, relation:aligned, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/57edb29d.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/57edb29d.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExtract the single plain rectangle and redraw it with the aligned rectangles' border-relative marker pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- The boundary color is the background/separator.\n- Foreground objects are dense rectangular regions; exactly one rectangle has only its base color.\n- Other rectangles contain their base color plus marker pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Crop the only plain rectangle; this crop is the output canvas.\n- Use marked rectangles whose row span overlaps the plain rectangle's row span.\n- Transfer their marker pixels by preserving each marker run's distance from the nearest rectangle edges.\n\nKey insight:\n- The marked rectangles are examples of an edge-relative pattern, so the missing plain rectangle receives the same pattern resized to its own dimensions.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"edge-relative marker run s in a marked rectangle aligned with the plain rectangle row band\",\n  \"dst\": \"run d in the plain rectangle crop\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.nearest_edge_offsets == d.nearest_edge_offsets\",\n  \"transform\": \"paint each matched d with the shared marker color; keep base rectangle fill elsewhere\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"same shape as the plain rectangle\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8f215267\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3507\nmechanism=0.4679\nlexical=0.0128\ncode_feature=0.2500\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8f215267.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8f215267.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nCount same-color patterns per frame and represent the tally as dots inside.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Hollow rectangular frames in various colors.\n- Small monochrome pattern sprites scattered outside frames.\n\nRule:\n- Remove all small patterns from the grid.\n- For each frame of color C, count how many patterns share color C.\n- Draw that many dots along the frame's center row, spaced by 2, starting from the right.\n\nKey insight: Frames act as tally displays — scattered same-color patterns are \"absorbed\" and their count is shown as interior dots.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"pattern sprites s outside frame sprites\",\n  \"dst\": \"fill hollow rectangular frame sprites d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"for each frame d: N = #{s | s.color == d.color}; draw N dots on mid-row(d), spaced by 2 from the right side\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e734a0e8\">\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
